"David Gale" <dsgSPAMFILTER@alum.dartmouth.org> writes:

> Of course, it's also a little unclear--it says, "Attempting to convert an
> altar by sacrificing at a non-coaligned altar _can_ convert *you* instead if
> your alignment is negative."  Should that 'can' be 'will' instead, for
> clarity?  That is, if your alignment is negative when you make the
> conversion attempt, will you always be converted, or is there just a
> percentage chance of it?  If it's guaranteed, I stand by my criticism of
> KPD; if it's a chance, could we get the specifics of that chance--and some
> mustard for flavor as I eat my hat?  :)  And what happens if your alignment
> is 0, as might be the case when trying to do the protection racket as KPD
> was?  (If it has to be negative, then I'd guess that he'd displaced his pet
> onto a trap at some point...)

It's guaranteed under normal circumstances - the exceptions are that
you can only convert yourself once in a game, and that you cannot
convert to Moloch (though you can convert an unaligned altar *outside*
of Gehennom).  If your alignment is 0, you will convert the altar as
normal.
